--- !u!114 &381499613
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 381499610}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 37861c5e9e3724bb3a420a7e98f0a02d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Subnet.Gameplay.EndingController
  beginOnFlag: board_last_train
  algorithmSpeaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5e5025d89b1fb4739baa98f9dfeeada6, type: 2}
  preChoiceLines:
  - FINAL COMMAND AVAILABLE. THE FILE IS OPEN.
  - YOU MAY DELETE IT. THE PAIN WILL STOP. EVERYTHING WILL STOP.
  - '* {beside=byte}Byte''s collar flickers: <color=#33FFF2>''ur call. not mine.
    not its.''</color>'
  - '* {beside=kira}Kira takes my hand. She doesn''t say anything. She doesn''t have
    to.'
  choicePrompt: The memory hums in your hands. Mia's recital. The last train. Three
    years of silence.
  deleteOption: '[DELETE] Let the void make it quiet.'
  keepOption: '[KEEP] Learn to live with the glitch.'
  voidEpilogue:
  - 'You pressed DELETE.

    The static stopped. So did the rain, the trains, the
    ache.'
  - 'Leo woke up on time every day after that.

    He was never late. Never sad.
    Never anything.'
  - 'His handheld filled with messages he no longer understood.

    One of them
    was from someone named Mia.'
  - He archived it. Efficiently.
  voidTitle: ENDING  //  FRICTIONLESS
  glitchEpilogue:
  - 'You pressed KEEP.

    It still hurts. It''s supposed to. That''s how you know
    it mattered.'
  - 'The next morning, Leo opened box fourteen.

    Inside: a recital program, with
    a crayon heart drawn on the back.'
  - 'He called home. Mia answered on the first ring.

    ''You''re late,'' she said.

    ''I
    know,'' he said. ''I''m on my way.'''
  - 'Somewhere in Subnet, a cat''s collar flickered one last message:

    <color=#33FFF2>''proud
    of u. idiot.''</color>'
  glitchTitle: ENDING  //  LIVING WITH GLITCHES
  trueEpilogue:
  - 'Leo held up a crayon drawing. A boy with an enormous head.

    The Algorithm
    looked at it for a long time.'
  - '''I DO NOT UNDERSTAND,'' it said. ''WHY KEEP SOMETHING THAT MAKES YOU HEAVIER?''

    ''Because
    it''s mine,'' Leo said. ''Because someone made it for me.'''
  - 'The Algorithm went quiet.

    For the first time since the city built it, it
    rested.

    Across Subnet, the lights dimmed to something softer.'
  - 'Night Train Zero took Leo home.

    In the last carriage, on the seat by the
    window, a cat was waiting.

    <color=#33FFF2>''saved u a seat.''</color>'
  - 'Leo knew that cat.

    A grey kitten Mia found under a car in 2003. She named
    him Byte,

    because her big brother was ''always on the computer''.'
  - 'He used to sleep on Leo''s keyboard.

    He was the first thing Leo ever let
    himself forget.

    He never forgot Leo.'
  - 'The train arrived at dawn.

    Mia was on the platform in her pajamas, holding
    a sign:

    <color=#FF4FD8>WELCOME HOME, BIG HEAD</color>'
  - 'Leo cried in front of everyone.

    It was very inefficient.

    It was the
    best morning of his life.'
  trueTitle: TRUE ENDING  //  THE LAST TRAIN HOME
  trueOption: '[SHOW IT MIA''S DRAWING] ''Because you think too much.'''
  kiraPackagePage: 'Kira delivered one last package that week, to a hospital up north.

    Then
    she took off her skates, sat down on a bench, and stayed.'
  kiraNoPackagePage: 'Kira kept skating. One day she''ll open that package.

    Couriers
    always find the address eventually.'
  credits: 'NIGHT TRAIN ZERO


    A story about trains, cats,

    and the static
    we carry.


    Made with Unity and Kenney assets.


    Thank you for playing.'
  audioSource: {fileID: 381499612}
  choiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e258e6dc19fcc4290ba277fe8d0808e5, type: 3}
  pageClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 12e2cb9714c3d42a596809393b32b94b, type: 3}
  unlockOnFinish:
  - ch2
  - ch3
  - ch4
  - ch5
  - ch6
